<p>Pinnacle Sales trains dealer teams on the lines they carry. The customer is the dealer. This is not a homeowner workshop and not a consumer class.</p>

<h2>What training already includes</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/faqs/">FAQs</a> already list hands-on sales training, showroom merchandising support, 2020/Winner design services, technical assistance, marketing resources, factory tours, and ongoing business development. This page does not add new programs. It points dealers to those existing services and to the <a href="/become-a-dealer/">application</a>.</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>In-person line training</strong> on the showroom floor for the brands you open.</li>
  <li><strong>Merchandising</strong> so displays sell Shiloh, Eclipse, Aspect, Vistora, and the rest of the six public brands you choose.</li>
  <li><strong>2020/Winner</strong> design and quoting support for complex specs. That claim is already on this site.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who to ask</h2>
<p><a href="/about/">Gillian Patriquin</a> is listed on About as Dealer &amp; Training Specialist, all territories, Northern Colorado. Territory sales still sit with the rep on your account. We do not invent extra titles or unpublished leads here.</p>

<h2>No public calendar</h2>
<p>There is no event listing on this page. We do not invent class dates, factory trip dates, or trade-show booths. If you want a showroom session or factory access, apply. Your rep schedules it. Factory context: <a href="/guides/ww-wood-factory/">WW Wood factory in Dudley</a>.</p>

<h2>Open a line, then train on it</h2>
<p>Custom shop or leaving a box line? Start with <a href="/guides/become-a-shiloh-dealer/">become a Shiloh dealer</a>. You do not have to take all six public brands. Training follows the lines you carry.</p>

</AeoGuide>
